            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0187" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20/667: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-26T19:00:00-04:00">May 26, 1938—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. In the past few days the American press has carried reports to the effect
                    that the German Government has ordered the withdrawal of the German military
                    mission from China and the stoppage of the shipment of German military supplies
                    to China. The Department would welcome such information in regard to these
                    reported developments as you may be able discreetly to obtain, together with
                    your comment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
